var free_video_and_paid_study_services_default = "---\nslug: free-video-and-paid-study-services\ntitle: How Mastemy's free video + paid study services model works\ndescription: Every lesson video on Mastemy is free to watch. Paid study packages cover original Mastemy study services only. Here is exactly where the line sits.\npublished: 2026-10-02\n---\n\nMastemy is built on one simple rule: **lesson videos are always free to watch**. Paying for something on Mastemy never unlocks a video, and no video is ever hidden behind a login.\n\n## The free part\n\nEvery published course on Mastemy is made of lessons, and each lesson's video plays through YouTube's official embedded player. That means:\n\n- You can open any lesson of a published course and watch it without an account and without paying.\n- Videos stay on YouTube and remain subject to YouTube's terms. Mastemy does not control the advertisements or recommendations YouTube shows.\n- If a video cannot play in the embedded player (for example because its owner disabled embedding), the lesson page explains why and offers a \"Watch on YouTube\" link.\n\nInstructors can also publish **free study notes** for a lesson. Those sit next to the video and do not require a purchase.\n\n## The paid part: study services\n\nInstructors may propose **study packages** for a course. A package sells original study services that Mastemy hosts, such as:\n\n- premium study notes written for the course,\n- larger or more advanced banks of multiple-choice practice questions,\n- mock or timed exams.\n\nEach package lists its included services in plain language on the course page, together with its price and access period. Packages are reviewed by Mastemy staff before they go on sale, and reviewers check that a package does not sell or unlock video access.\n\n## What an account adds\n\nA free account lets you keep private notes on lessons, save your watch position, take practice questions and track your progress. None of this changes whether you can watch the video.\n\n## Why we work this way\n\nVideo teaching is most useful when anyone can reach it. The study services are where Mastemy and its instructors add work that goes beyond the video: structured notes, reviewed questions with explanations for every option, and assessments. Keeping the two apart lets you judge a course by watching it first, and decide later whether the extra study services are worth it to you.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- Browse the [free video lessons](/free-lessons).\n- Read what [study packages](/packages) contain and what they never include.\n- See [how MCQ certificates work](/articles/how-mcq-certificates-work).\n";
//#endregion
//#region src/content/articles/how-mcq-certificates-work.md?raw
var how_mcq_certificates_work_default = "---\nslug: how-mcq-certificates-work\ntitle: How our MCQ certificates work and what they do and don't prove\ndescription: A Mastemy certificate confirms that its holder passed an approved multiple-choice knowledge assessment. It does not certify practical competence or replace any external certification.\npublished: 2026-10-02\n---\n\nSome Mastemy courses end with an assessment that counts toward a certificate. This article explains how that certificate is earned, how anyone can check it, and, just as important, what it does **not** say about its holder.\n\n## How a certificate is earned\n\n1. The course includes one or more assessments that the instructor marked as counting toward the certificate.\n2. Those assessments are built from multiple-choice questions. Questions go through review before they become active, and every option carries an explanation shown after the attempt.\n3. The learner takes the assessment. Timed exams use the server's clock, and grading happens on the server, not in the browser.\n4. If the score meets the pass threshold set for the assessment, Mastemy issues a certificate with a unique code.\n\n## How anyone can verify it\n\nEach certificate has a code. Anyone, such as an employer, can enter it on the [verification page](/verify) to see whether it was issued by Mastemy, who it was issued to, for which course, when, and whether it has since been revoked.\n\n## What a certificate proves\n\nA valid Mastemy certificate shows that its holder **passed an MCQ knowledge assessment** for a specific course on a specific date.\n\n## What it does not prove\n\n- It does **not** verify practical, hands-on or professional competence. Multiple-choice questions test knowledge and reasoning, not the ability to carry out a task in a real setting.\n- It is **not** an official certification from any exam body, professional association or government. Where a Mastemy course prepares for an external certification, passing the Mastemy assessment does not grant that certification.\n- It does **not** record how much of the course video was watched. Watch progress is saved only as a convenience and never affects certificates.\n\n## Why we are explicit about this\n\nA credential is only useful if people can trust what it means. By stating the limits plainly on the certificate, the verification page and here, we hope employers and learners can give a Mastemy certificate exactly the weight it deserves, no more and no less.\n";
//#endregion
//#region src/content/articles/prepare-for-a-certification-exam.md?raw
var prepare_for_a_certification_exam_default = "---\nslug: prepare-for-a-certification-exam\ntitle: How to prepare with Mastemy for a certification exam\ndescription: A practical way to use Mastemy's certification directory, preparation courses, practice questions and coverage information when studying for an external exam.\npublished: 2026-10-02\n---\n\nMany learners use Mastemy to study for an external certification exam. Mastemy is **not** the exam provider and does not claim any partnership with, or endorsement by, the bodies that run these exams. This guide explains how to use what Mastemy does offer.\n\n## 1. Start from the official source\n\nOpen the certification in the [certification directory](/certifications). Each entry shows the issuer, exam code, version, the date Mastemy staff last checked the details, and a link to the **official source**. Always read the official page first: it is the authority on eligibility, fees, exam format and the current syllabus. If the official information differs from what you see on Mastemy, the official information is correct.\n\nEntries are only listed publicly after a reviewer has checked them recently. If an entry has not been re-checked for too long, it is removed from the public directory until someone checks it again.\n\n## 2. Read the blueprint and any non-MCQ disclosure\n\nWhere available, the entry lists the exam's objectives with their weights. Use the weights to plan your time. If the real exam includes tasks that are not multiple-choice (such as practical labs, essays or simulations), the entry says so. Mastemy's practice is multiple-choice, so plan separate practice for those parts.\n\n## 3. Choose a preparation course\n\nThe entry lists live Mastemy courses mapped to that certification. Every lesson video in those courses is free to watch. Work through the lessons in the order the course suggests and take notes as you go.\n\n## 4. Practise actively\n\nUse the practice questions attached to lessons and modules. Read the explanation for every option, including the ones you got right. Come back to topics where you were unsure.\n\n## 5. Check yourself under exam conditions\n\nIf the course offers timed exams, take one only after you have finished the material, and treat the result as a signal of which objectives to revisit, not as a prediction of your real exam score.\n\n## 6. Keep the limits in mind\n\n- Passing a Mastemy assessment does not grant the external certification.\n- Exam syllabi change. Check the \"last checked\" date and the official source shortly before you book your exam.\n- A Mastemy certificate confirms a passed MCQ knowledge assessment only. See [what our certificates do and don't prove](/articles/how-mcq-certificates-work).\n";
